    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/science">science</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · Phys.org · 2026-11-05 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Avian Influenza Outbreak Spreads to Mammals on Illinois Farm</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A highly pathogenic avian influenza outbreak that decimated a backyard flock in Illinois has spread to a domestic cat and wild rats, according to analysis by the University of Illinois and the University of Missouri. Researchers confirmed the mammals were infected with the same H5N1 subtype found in the poultry, likely through scavenging carcasses.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/avian-influenza-outbreak-spreads-to-mammals-on-illinois-farm.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Viral genomic sequencing revealed nearly identical sequences across all three species, with mammalian-adaptation mutations detected in the samples. Experts suggest that wild rats, which live close to livestock and feed, may serve as an overlooked link in virus transmission between wild birds and domestic environments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the key findings of the H5N1 transmission study, including the specific animal hosts and the significance of the genomic findings.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://phys.org/news/2026-11-avian-influenza-backyard-coop-illinois.html" rel="noopener">Phys.org</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
