       <h1>Blue Origin Delays New Glenn Launch to 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Blue Origin has rescheduled the next launch of its New Glenn rocket to January 2027. CEO Dave Limp confirmed the timeline in an internal memo, citing bad weather and necessary repairs following a May launchpad explosion that damaged facilities previously intended for an Amazon satellite mission.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/blue-origin-delays-new-glenn-launch-to-2027.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While founder Jeff Bezos had previously targeted a December window, the new date represents a roughly 10-day delay from earlier projections. Limp emphasized that returning New Glenn to flight remains the company's primary focus, noting that the adjustment does not undermine the team's ongoing progress or the importance of the work ahead.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and concise, capturing the essential delay and the context of the launchpad damage.</p>
