       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Four Fishermen Found Dead Following Boat Capsizing off Andhra Coast</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Four fishermen from Tamil Nadu have been confirmed dead after their boat capsized 2 km off the coast of Adani Krishnapatnam Port. Three bodies washed ashore at Kothapatnam beach, while a fourth was recovered by the Indian Coast Guard near Nizampatnam Port.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/four-fishermen-found-dead-following-boat-capsizing-off-andhr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The vessel was carrying nine fishermen when it encountered intense winds and a storm at sea on November 3. The Indian Coast Guard is currently utilizing a Dornier aircraft and coordinating with Chennai authorities to conduct a search and rescue operation for the five remaining missing crew members.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the casualty figures and rescue efforts, though it identifies the port of the boat's capsizing correctly per the text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/bodies-of-four-fishermen-from-tn-found-near-kothapatnam-beach-in-ap/article71670219.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
