     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Universities Miss Top 50 in QS Asia Rankings 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#QS Asia Rankings</span> <span>#Indian Universities</span> <span>#IITs</span> <span>#Education</span></div>
       <p>The QS Asia Rankings 2027 have been released, revealing that no Indian university has secured a position within the top 50. This outcome marks a significant concern for the country's higher education sector.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/indian-universities-miss-top-50-in-qs-asia-rankings-2027.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This is the second consecutive year that Indian universities have failed to place within the top 50 of the prestigious QS Asia Rankings. The consistent absence highlights ongoing challenges in global competitiveness.</p><p>Furthermore, the rankings indicate a decline for the Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs), which have slipped further in their positions. This trend suggests a broader issue affecting some of India's most prominent technical institutions.</p><p>What to watch: Future strategies to improve global university rankings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a concise and accurate summary of the provided source snippet.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-_?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
