     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-05 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Interstate Marijuana Trafficking Ring Busted in Cyberabad</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Five members of an Assam-based gang were arrested following a 60-day hunt by the EAGLE Force for operating an interstate marijuana trafficking network. Led by former security guard Bhaskar Hazarika, the group transported consignments from Odisha to Hyderabad, moving approximately 400 kg of marijuana over 10 months and generating nearly ₹1.8 crore in sales.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/interstate-marijuana-trafficking-ring-busted-in-cyberabad.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The network utilized a distribution model where each kilogram was divided into 150 small packets sold for ₹300 each to a base of 100 regular consumers. Authorities seized 24.7 kg of marijuana and seven mobile phones during the operation, which involved coordinated efforts with the Choutuppal Police.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and captures all key figures and operational details from the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/former-security-guard-operates-drug-network-telanganas-eagle-force-arresst-gang-after-60-day-hunt/article71669614.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
