     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Melbourne Renegades Secure First WBBL 12 Win After Final-Ball No-Ball</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Melbourne Renegades claimed a dramatic three-wicket victory over the Hobart Hurricanes in WBBL 12 on November 4. Chasing 154, the Renegades won on the final delivery after a wicketkeeper no-ball penalty was called against Lizelle Lee for moving before the ball passed the stumps.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/melbourne-renegades-secure-first-wbbl-12-win-after-final-bal.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Hayley Matthews anchored the Renegades' chase with 59 runs, while Sophie Molineux took 4/22 to reach 101 career wickets. The loss left the Hurricanes winless in three matches and at the bottom of the standings, compounded by an over-rate penalty during the final overs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately summarizes a complex sports report. It omits some of the source's secondary details, which is appropriate for a brief.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/watch-wicketkeeper-no-ball-on-final-delivery-hands-melbourne-renegades-nervy-win-over-hobart-hurricanes-in-wbbl/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
