     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-11-05 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pennsylvania Couple Wins Legal Battle Over Public Steps Maintenance</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Pennsylvania Commonwealth Court has ruled that the Borough of Jim Thorpe is responsible for maintaining the High Street Steps, a passage connecting two public roads. The decision in TM Loughery and MK Loughery v. Borough of Jim Thorpe affirms that 130 years of public use and historical borough involvement in repairs established the steps as public property.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/pennsylvania-couple-wins-legal-battle-over-public-steps-main.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Although the borough argued that no formal ordinance accepted the steps, the court found sufficient evidence of long-term public access and municipal funding for construction and maintenance. The ruling concludes a legal dispute that began in 2019, ultimately requiring the borough to maintain the stairs situated on private and municipal land.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report accurately conveys the court ruling and the reasoning behind the borough's maintenance obligations based on historical usage and municipal actions.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-couple-fought-to-make-their-town-maintain-public-steps-that-cross-their-private-land-after-evidence-of-130-years-of-public-use-and-repairs-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-boroughs-duty-to-maintain-them/articleshow/135535744.cms" rel="noopener">Times of India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
