     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-11-05 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>PoJK Sit-In: JAAC Leader Alleges ISI-Linked Weapon Recovery, Covert Sabotage Plot</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#PoJK</span> <span>#Umar Nazir Kashmiri</span> <span>#ISI</span> <span>#Protests</span></div>
       <p>Tensions in Pakistan-occupied Jammu and Kashmir (PoJK) have escalated following explosive allegations by Joint Awami Action Committee (JAAC) leader Umar Nazir Kashmiri. Addressing an ongoing sit-in in Rawalakot, Kashmiri accused the Pakistani military apparatus of orchestrating covert operations to destabilize peaceful demonstrations and create pretexts for violent crackdowns. These claims surfaced after the recovery of a weapon at the protest site, which reportedly bore ink-written markings and a sticker explicitly linking it to Pakistan’s Inter-Services Intelligence (ISI).</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/pojk-sit-in-jaac-leader-alleges-isi-linked-weapon-recovery-c.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Kashmiri stated that a video documenting the seized weapon and its markings would be released soon to expose what he described as a state-sponsored conspiracy. He alleged that three armed operatives, dressed in plain clothes, infiltrated the sit-in two days prior with a plan to open fire on both protesters and security forces before fleeing. The objective, he claimed, was to trigger widespread chaos and provide authorities with a justification for a lethal crackdown. Furthermore, the JAAC leader revealed that over the past five days, unidentified individuals, reportedly under armed protection, accumulated waste and attempted to dump it into a cold settlement area near the protest camp, actions Kashmiri asserted were coordinated provocations aimed at disrupting the peaceful assembly and inciting conflict.</p><p>Kashmiri issued a stern warning that terrorists operating in civilian attire are being deployed to target both demonstrators and forces, with the intent of orchestrating further bloodshed. He framed the ongoing violence as a calculated campaign designed to crush the civil rights movement in the region.</p><p>In a defiant response to the deaths of three young Kashmiri men—identified as Adil, Atif, and Ehtisham—Umar Nazir Kashmiri declared that the community would not let their sacrifices be in vain. He vowed to pursue justice and accountability, announcing the suspension of scheduled funeral prayers as an act of defiance against state oppression. Instead of immediate burial, the bodies of the victims are being brought directly to the sit-in location, and demonstrators have been urged to gather in silent protest around the fallen youths, signaling a hardening of resolve across PoJK as the confrontation between local citizens and the administration intensifies.</p><p>What to watch: Further developments surrounding the alleged sabotage and community response in PoJK.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report captures the gravity of the allegations and the specific details regarding the protest actions and victim names as reported in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/pojk-sit-in-sabotage-plot-umar-nazir-kashmiri-claims-isi-marked-weapon-recovered-in-rawalakot-exclusive-details-ws-lr-10414727.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
