     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-11-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana Achieves Record-Breaking Rs. 50 Crore Opening Day Amid Pre-Diwali Period</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Box Office</span> <span>#Ramayana</span> <span>#Ranbir Kapoor</span></div>
       <p>The film Ramayana, starring Ranbir Kapoor and Yash, has achieved a phenomenal start at the Hindi box office, with early estimates indicating a first-day business ranging from Rs. 50 crore to Rs. 51 crore. This figure is contingent on the film's performance in the single screens of the mass belt. This remarkable opening establishes Ramayana as the biggest pre-Diwali start, shattering the long-standing record previously held by the Salman Khan-led Tiger 3, which opened at Rs. 44 crore on Diwali day.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/ramayana-achieves-record-breaking-rs-50-crore-opening-day-am.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While a dip in business is anticipated on Friday, projections suggest that Saturday's figures could potentially surpass the opening day, even reaching the Rs. 60 crore mark, driven by overwhelmingly positive reports. The four-day pre-Diwali weekend for Ramayana is expected to accumulate around Rs. 210 crore. Following this, the film is projected to peak from Monday to Wednesday, potentially doubling its pre-Diwali total. The business performance is described as phenomenal across the board, with Ranbir Kapoor and Yash showcasing their star power even during what is typically a lull period.</p><p>National cinema chains are estimated to have collected approximately Rs. 30 crore on Thursday, contributing 55 percent to the film's total opening day business. Ramayana has received a wide release, with over 20,000 shows in North India, and peak capacity is expected to be achieved on Monday. It is worth noting that the film had a limited release in the South by distributor partners, a factor that reportedly cost it at least Rs. 5 crore in Hindi business.</p><p>What to watch: The film's sustained performance through the extended holiday period.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft synthesizes the box office estimates and context provided in the source text accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-day-one-box-office-estimate-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-create-history-smash-all-pre-diwali-records-with-a-monstrous-rs-50-crore-opening/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
