     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-11-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana Advance Booking: Ranbir Kapoor and Yash starrer collects Rs. 20 crores</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Box Office</span> <span>#Entertainment</span></div>
       <p>The upcoming mythological epic Ramayana has generated significant pre-release momentum, with advance bookings reaching Rs. 20 crores by 12 noon on the day of reporting. According to Bollywood Hungama, this massive response indicates strong audience anticipation for the project, which features Ranbir Kapoor as Lord Ram and Yash as Ravana.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/ramayana-advance-booking-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-starrer-coll.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Among major cities, Bengaluru leads the advance sales, contributing Rs. 1.23 crores gross (Rs. 1.07 crores nett) from 25,196 tickets sold across 222 shows, maintaining an occupancy rate of 34.1%. Mumbai follows with Rs. 67.47 lakhs gross (Rs. 58.70 lakhs nett) from 14,782 tickets across 334 shows and an occupancy of 18.7%. Hyderabad ranks third, with 26,846 tickets sold across 162 shows, achieving the highest occupancy rate among top cities at 40.8% and contributing Rs. 53.98 lakhs gross (Rs. 46.96 lakhs nett).</p><p>Regional data shows the NCR netting Rs. 93.97 lakhs gross (Rs. 81.76 lakhs nett) from 18,677 tickets, while Karnataka collected Rs. 81.07 lakhs gross (Rs. 70.53 lakhs nett) with 30,303 tickets. Maharashtra contributed Rs. 79.74 lakhs gross (Rs. 69.37 lakhs nett) from 24,706 tickets across 839 shows. In the multiplex sector, PVR holds the lead with Rs. 2.52 crores gross (Rs. 2.19 crores nett) across 789 shows, followed by INOX with Rs. 2.07 crores gross (Rs. 1.80 crores nett) across 799 shows.</p><p>While final opening-day figures remain dependent on walk-in audiences and the progression of bookings, the initial data suggests a powerful start for the film. The scale of the project and the casting choices are cited as primary drivers of interest. The coming hours are expected to be critical in determining the film's final opening-day potential.</p><p>What to watch: Final opening-day box office figures and sustained multiplex occupancy rates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the detailed statistical data provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-advance-booking-ranbir-kapoor-yash-starrer-collects-rs-20-crores-till-12-noon-massive-ticket-sales-point-to-a-bumper-opening/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
