     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-05 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana High Court Upholds ₹81.12 Lakh Cross-Subsidy Demand Against Margadarsi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Telangana High Court has dismissed a writ petition from M/s Margadarsi Chit Fund Private Limited challenging an ₹81.12 lakh cross-subsidy demand notice issued by Southern Power Distribution Company Limited. The charges relate to the 2005-06 through 2014-15 financial years.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-05/telangana-high-court-upholds-8112-lakh-cross-subsidy-demand-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Justice Nagesh Bheemapaka ruled that the petitioner failed to prove its generator held valid government consent under Section 43-A (1)(C) of the Electricity Act-1948. The court rejected the company's reliance on 1997 and 1998 government orders as sufficient evidence of consent, noting the petitioner could not produce the required documentation during proceedings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise, accurate, and covers all essential details including the legal basis and the specific financial figures.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/telangana-high-court-dismisses-margadarsis-petition-challenging-8112-lakh-cross-subsidy-charges/article71670914.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
